        "symbol": "SP500",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "Book flat at GBP 1,500 with zero positions; no directional SP500 thesis has matured, so hold stands. Fresh quote (bid 7690.6 / ask 7691.1, quote_time 1792483327) has drifted below the prior decision's 7696.7 and sits below both the 20-session SMA (7736.94) and the 50-session SMA (7705.23), with RSI 48.2 and a negative MACD histogram (-11.24) — a mild continuation of the rate-capped grind, resolving only a pricing objection and triggering nothing. The shared restrictive-rates-plus-energy factor remains verified but not directionally resolved: the delivered FOMC minutes extract (e4ca17945c0d6c56) and FOMC statement (c4766cd2c8ccfd44) confirm the Fed hiked 12-0 to 3.75-4.00% with inflation elevated, while the readable BoE MPC summary (6c6b04263fe1e72b) shows a 6-3 hold with three hike votes and upside CPI risk. The ~89bp 2y-over-funds gap is still undecomposed — no OIS strip, consensus or positioning exists — and the credit question (HY widening versus calm BBB/NFCI per the committee's correlation double-counting caution) is unresolved pending multi-session breadth. The decisive catalysts land within 48 hours: UK unemployment today (Oct 20) and UK CPI tomorrow (Oct 21). Today's BBC flow is unverified single-publisher material; the 'job vacancies fall as small firms cut back on recruitment' item (c1fb64abaf970055), if corroborated by the ONS release, would soften the UK second-round hawkish case rather than resolve the US index factor. Initiating now would express one shared factor before its scheduled test. Long financing remains ~-0.16 GBP per 0.1 lot daily (~-1.12 over seven days), metadata not measured economics against an unproven thesis.",
        "thesis": "Hold on SP500 is a portfolio-level decision, unchanged from the three prior approved holds. Verified standing facts: Fed target 3.75-4.00% from a 12-0 hike (c4766cd2c8ccfd44), corroborated by readable FOMC minutes text noting inflation elevated, geopolitical energy pressure and the 'will deliver price stability' commitment (e4ca17945c0d6c56); BoE Bank Rate 3.75% (119ab1d3fbfe56ef) held 6-3 with three hike dissents, CPI 3.1% in August likely rising further, and the MPC judging inflation risks tilted upside (6c6b04263fe1e72b, 3257cb6a1f95a005); UK unemployment 4.9% May-Jul (f86574b608ca7c64) stays soft; long-end rates easing modestly (DGS30 5.43%: f9cbbbf409ae00f6); Brent $126.55 sustaining the energy-inflation channel (f0649cf2ac4fbbe7). The falsifiable question is unchanged: does the shared global-tightening factor keep compressing long-duration index multiples, or does range trade persist with intact labour and calm aggregate credit? The Oct 20 UK labour print (with today's unverified BBC vacancy report as a possible softening preview) and the Oct 21 CPI print are the scheduled tests of the second-round branch. The current quote below both SMAs with a negative MACD histogram is diagnostic of neither hypothesis. No order is warranted; any future conversion additionally requires fresh quotes, measured CFD costs and decomposed policy expectations.",
        "countercase": "Strongest case against holding: the short-side branch is half-confirmed — the index sits below both SMAs with a negative MACD histogram, HY OAS has widened materially over 20 sessions while the Fed hikes and the BoE leans hawkish with upside CPI risk — so waiting through two scheduled UK prints forgoes trend if discount-rate compression accelerates. Strongest case against a short is equally concrete: Monday's rebound snapshots (QQQ +1.37%, MU +3.07%) cut against the stress narrative, HY at ~3.31% remains historically tight, BBB near 1.06% and deeply loose NFCI show no systemic strain, and the committee has established that VIX, HY OAS and Friday's heavy QQQ volume are one correlated cluster, not independent confirmations — shorting now risks expressing a single unresolved event. A third objection: a flat GBP 1,500 demo book forgoes learning. That is outweighed by the mandate's patient-thesis requirement and by catalysts arriving within 48 hours that can move every watch file simultaneously through the shared factor; a six-hour-plus hold is an ordinary minimum, not a timer.",
        "invalidation": "Hold converts to a directional file only with specific source-backed resolution: (1) the Oct 21 UK CPI print — confirmed second-round wage/price effects escalate the global-tightening branch; an energy-only rise with soft labour weakens it; (2) HY OAS sustained above ~3.5-3.6% with continued high-volume breadth losses would justify researching a short index file; (3) the 10y below ~4.9% with HY back under ~3.0% and index volume normalising would close the rate-compression line and justify researching a long file; (4) readable OIS/SEP decomposition separating expected policy from term premium. New price levels alone resolve only pricing objections and never trigger trades. Any conversion requires fresh-session quotes, measured spread and a full holding-cost budget; the instrument is a price-only CFD with swap fields as metadata. Uncertified full-filing diligence may justify continued holding even where a directional thesis matures. If today's ONS release confirms the BBC vacancy softening with corroborated wage detail, the GBP second-round branch weakens and the shared-factor escalation case narrows further.",
